---

---

<figure class="diagram">
	<svg
		class="diagram-narrow"
		viewBox="-2 0 356 524"
		role="img"
		aria-label="With the mouse still, the loop keeps turning by itself"
	>
		<defs>
			<marker
				id="loop-narrow-arrow"
				viewBox="0 0 10 10"
				refX="9"
				refY="5"
				markerWidth="6"
				markerHeight="6"
				orient="auto-start-reverse"
			>
				<path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="diagram-arrowhead"></path>
			</marker>
			<marker
				id="loop-narrow-fix-arrow"
				viewBox="0 0 10 10"
				refX="9"
				refY="5"
				markerWidth="6"
				markerHeight="6"
				orient="auto-start-reverse"
			>
				<path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="diagram-accent-fill"></path>
			</marker>
		</defs>
		<text x="0" y="22" class="diagram-title">With the mouse still,</text>
		<text x="0" y="42" class="diagram-title"
			>the loop keeps turning by itself</text
		>
		<g class="diagram-line">
			<path d="M150 128V152" marker-end="url(#loop-narrow-arrow)"></path>
			<path d="M150 216V240" marker-end="url(#loop-narrow-arrow)"></path>
			<path d="M150 304V328" marker-end="url(#loop-narrow-arrow)"></path>
		</g>
		<path
			d="M300 360H332V96H300"
			class="diagram-accent-line"
			marker-end="url(#loop-narrow-fix-arrow)"></path>
		<rect x="0" y="64" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="16" y="90" class="diagram-name">1. Preview moves the card</text>
		<text x="16" y="112" class="diagram-body"
			>onDragOver calls setDragBoard</text
		>
		<rect x="0" y="152" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="16" y="178" class="diagram-name"
			>2. React re-renders, layout shifts</text
		>
		<text x="16" y="200" class="diagram-body">Cards in both columns shift</text>
		<rect x="0" y="240" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="16" y="266" class="diagram-name">3. dnd-kit measures again</text>
		<text x="16" y="288" class="diagram-body"
			>Runs even though the mouse is still</text
		>
		<rect x="0" y="328" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="16" y="354" class="diagram-name"
			>4. The other column is now closest</text
		>
		<text x="16" y="376" class="diagram-body"
			>So onDragOver moves the card back</text
		>
		<text x="0" y="424" class="diagram-note-strong"
			>The blue line back to 1 is the fix:</text
		>
		<text x="0" y="442" class="diagram-note-strong"
			>skip if this frame already moved a card.</text
		>
		<text x="0" y="478" class="diagram-body"
			>About 6 ms per turn. Turn after turn,</text
		>
		<text x="0" y="496" class="diagram-body"
			>React counts nested updates until it</text
		>
		<text x="0" y="514" class="diagram-body">gives up.</text>
	</svg>
	<svg
		class="diagram-wide"
		viewBox="0 0 760 340"
		role="img"
		aria-label="With the mouse still, the loop keeps turning by itself"
	>
		<defs>
			<marker
				id="loop-arrow"
				viewBox="0 0 10 10"
				refX="9"
				refY="5"
				markerWidth="6"
				markerHeight="6"
				orient="auto-start-reverse"
			>
				<path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="diagram-arrowhead"></path>
			</marker>
			<marker
				id="loop-fix-arrow"
				viewBox="0 0 10 10"
				refX="9"
				refY="5"
				markerWidth="6"
				markerHeight="6"
				orient="auto-start-reverse"
			>
				<path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="diagram-accent-fill"></path>
			</marker>
		</defs>
		<text x="24" y="34" class="diagram-title">
			With the mouse still, the loop keeps turning by itself
		</text>
		<g class="diagram-line">
			<path d="M340 110H420" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)"></path>
			<path d="M570 142V218" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)"></path>
			<path d="M420 250H340" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)"></path>
		</g>
		<path
			d="M190 218V142"
			class="diagram-accent-line"
			marker-end="url(#loop-fix-arrow)"></path>
		<text x="204" y="184" class="diagram-note-strong">
			The fix: skip if this frame already moved a card
		</text>
		<rect x="40" y="78" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="56" y="104" class="diagram-name"> 1. Preview moves the card </text>
		<text x="56" y="126" class="diagram-body">
			onDragOver calls setDragBoard
		</text>
		<rect x="420" y="78" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="436" y="104" class="diagram-name">
			2. React re-renders, layout shifts
		</text>
		<text x="436" y="126" class="diagram-body">
			Cards in both columns shift
		</text>
		<rect x="420" y="218" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="436" y="244" class="diagram-name">
			3. dnd-kit measures again
		</text>
		<text x="436" y="266" class="diagram-body">
			Runs even though the mouse is still
		</text>
		<rect x="40" y="218" width="300" height="64" rx="8" class="diagram-box"
		></rect>
		<text x="56" y="244" class="diagram-name">
			4. The other column is now closest
		</text>
		<text x="56" y="266" class="diagram-body">
			So onDragOver moves the card back
		</text>
		<text x="24" y="318" class="diagram-body">
			About 6 ms per turn. Turn after turn, React counts nested updates until it
			gives up.
		</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		The drag preview loop. The fix sits on the step from 4 back to 1.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
